# Enforce Platform Admin approval for ANY production infrastructure or configuration changes
# ADR-037 #6: every prod overlay directory requires explicit Platform Engineering
# review. Only the first of these three was listed, leaving 8 files under the two
# spoke prod overlays modifiable without the mandated approval.
#
# Patterns are recursive (trailing /) rather than /*, which in CODEOWNERS matches
# only files directly in the directory and silently skips any subdirectory added later.
/manifests/environments/prod/ @soloz-io/platform-admins
/manifests/spoke/spoke-pools/prod/ @soloz-io/platform-admins
# The catalogue no longer has an environment axis (ADR-051 amendment 2026-09-18):
# platform content splits by provider and nothing else, so there is no prod/
# directory to guard. The whole catalogue is guarded instead -- it reaches every
# spoke on every box, which is a wider blast radius than prod's overlay had.
/manifests/spoke/spoke-catalog/ @soloz-io/platform-admins
